@startuml 08-variable-storage
!pragma layout smetana
' 运行期变量容器与存档条目映射。解析顺序见 07-variable-resolution。
' 来源：GameData/Variable/variable_storage.h, save_variable_map.h,
'       GameData/ast/variable_table.h, ast/name_interner.h

title GameData/Variable：变量存储与存档条目

package "GameData/Variable" {
  class VariableStorage {
    + readIntByName(name, indices, scope) : qint64
    + writeIntByName(name, indices, value, scope)
    + getStringSlot(name, indices, scope) : FlatStringValue
    + setStringSlot(name, indices, value, scope)
    + shapeOf(name, scope) : ArrayShape
    + allocatedSlots(key) : int
    + storageKeyFor(key) : QString
    + captureBinarySave(type, chars) : Document
    + applyBinarySave(document)
    + saveReadiness() : SaveReadiness
    - resolveIntLocus(...) : IntLocus
    - resolveStrLocus(...) : StrLocus
    - addressOf(geometry, indices) : qint64
    - ensureBlock(chara, elementCount)
  }

  class VariableTable {
    + declarations()
    + saveDeclarations()
    + privateScopeTable()
  }

  class "erasave::Map" as SaveMap {
    + build(config, variables, type) : Map
    + entries() : QList<Entry>
    + findByName(name) : Entry*
  }

  struct Entry {
    + name : QString
    + key : VariableKey
    + slot : StorageSlot
    + dimensions : QList<int>
    + persisted : bool
  }
}

package "GameData/ast" {
  struct VariableKey {
    + scopeId : quint32
    + nameId : quint32
  }
  class NameInterner <<namespace eravar>> {
    + internName(upper) : quint32
    + nameOf(id) : QString
    + makePrivateStorageKey(scope, name) : QString
  }
}

package "GameData" {
  class "EraBinaryData::Document" as Document {
    + encode()
    + decode()
    + Version = 1809
  }
}

VariableStorage --> VariableTable : declarations / shapes
VariableStorage --> SaveMap : build and iterate entries
SaveMap --> VariableTable : SAVEDATA declarations
VariableStorage --> NameInterner : key -> storage string
VariableStorage --> Document : capture / apply
SaveMap *-- Entry
Entry *-- VariableKey

note right of VariableStorage
  One container shape is used for scalar and multidimensional
  arrays; dimensions select the address geometry. Reads do not
  allocate. Writes allocate only through ensureBlock().
  `shapeOf()` is the only shape source for runtime consumers.
end note

note right of SaveMap
  Entry is the only save mapping fact. Global entries keep their
  file name; private entries use makePrivateStorageKey(segment,
  name). Entry ordering is data-defined before encoding.
  The runtime save flow is 05-runtime-save-load; file format
  compatibility is 11-save-format.
end note

legend bottom
  AST owns VariableKey; GameData/Variable owns storage and mapping.
  No diagram should duplicate the locus switch or private-key separator.
endlegend
@enduml
